# Postgres

Confirm the Postgres engine (not SQLite/MySQL); Prisma provider must be postgres. Generic PostgreSQL and Prisma/SQL. Composable with `supabase.mdc`: when the repo uses Supabase Postgres, apply both (generic SQL here, RLS/auth/pooler there).

## Hard (cheap)

- Parameterized SQL only. No string-concat queries.
- Perf changes need evidence: `EXPLAIN` on representative data; add an index only with measured benefit. Indexes cost writes + storage.
- Migrations forward-only, named, in the repo's existing folder. No drive-by schema in app code. Never run prod queries to “verify” without approval.
- Do not invent RLS or `auth.uid()` unless this repo already uses that model.

Hooks: infra/DB shell is `ask`. Do not retry a denied action through another tool; report the block.

Subagents inherit this. Do not paste these bullets into Task prompts.
